WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:56.000
In 1870, a 19-year-old named Samuel Burke Burnett bought 100 head of cattle, wearing the brand, 6, 6, 6, wait for it, 6. And the legend says that he won the ranch with 4-6s in a poker game, but that's not true. And the fact that everyone repeats it anyway tells you the ranch was in the business of myth before it was in the business of cattle, like most of the West. And Burnett built an empire on grass, and a good deal of that grass belonged to the Camantric. and to understand how a Texas cattleman ended up grazing his herds on a Comanche reservation, you have to know who Quana Parker was. In 1836, Comanche Raiders hit Fort Parker in East Texas and carried off a nine-year-old girl named Cynthia Ann Parker. She grew up at Comanche, married the war leader, Petta Nakona, and had children.
1870年，一位名叫塞缪尔·伯克·伯内特（Samuel Burke Burnett）的19岁年轻人买了100头牛，并给它们打上了烙印：6、6、6，等等，还有个6。传说他是在一场扑克游戏中赢得了这个牧场，赢牌是四个6，但这并非事实。然而，每个人都在重复这个故事，这本身就说明，在成为养牛场之前，这个牧场就已经成了神话的载体，就像美国西部的大多数地方一样。伯内特靠草场建立了一个帝国，而这些草场中有很大一部分属于科曼奇人。要理解一个德克萨斯州的牧牛人是如何在科曼奇人的保留地上放牧的，你必须了解夸纳·帕克（Quana Parker）是谁。1836年，科曼奇突袭者袭击了东德克萨斯的帕克堡，带走了一个名叫辛西娅·安·帕克（Cynthia Ann Parker）的九岁女孩。她在科曼奇部落长大，嫁给了战争领袖佩塔·纳科纳（Petta Nakona），并生下了孩子。

