00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:52.000
And when Texas Rangers recaptured her in 1860, she never had a man. adjusted to white life again, and she tried to go back to the Indians. Her story is the loose source for the movie The Searchers, John Ford's 1956 Western, one of the most famous films ever made about a white family's obsession with a captive who doesn't want to be rescued. Her son was Quana, and he grew up to lead the Quadi, the hardest holdout Comanche band. He fought the buffalo hunters at Adobe Walls in 1874. And in 1875, he became the last Comanche leader to bring his people onto the reservation at Fort Sill. What Quana did next is why he belongs in an episode about Taylor Sheridan's movie and TV show universe centered around his hit Yellowstone.
当德克萨斯骑警在1860年将她夺回时，她再也没有适应白人的生活，并试图回到印第安人身边。她的故事是约翰·福特1956年的西部片《搜索者》（The Searchers）的松散素材来源，这是有史以来关于一个白人家庭执着于寻找一个不想被营救的被俘者的最著名电影之一。她的儿子是夸纳，他长大后领导了夸哈迪（Quadi）部落，这是科曼奇人中最顽固的抵抗派。1874年，他在Adobe Walls与水牛猎人作战。1875年，他成为最后一位带领族人进入锡尔堡（Fort Sill）保留地的科曼奇领袖。夸纳接下来所做的事情，就是他为什么会出现在这一集关于泰勒·谢里丹（Taylor Sheridan）的电影和电视宇宙（以他热门剧集《黄石》为中心）中的原因。

